<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cuffy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1763">1763</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Coffy, Kofi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cuffy, or Coffy, was an enslaved man of West African origin who led the Berbice slave uprising in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colony of Berbice, in present-day Guyana. The revolt began on 23 February 1763, and the rebels held most of the colony for nearly a year before Dutch troops suppressed it; Cuffy died during the rising amid divisions among its leaders. He is Guyana's national hero, and the uprising's anniversary is its Republic Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cuffy.jpg" alt="Cuffy" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Stanley · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1763_Monument,_Georgetown,_Guyana._2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
